  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "FFmpeg 9.0.1 - \"Lei\"\n\t\t\tVersion numbering scheme changed: FFMpegMajor.Major.Minor.Patch\n\n\t\t\t--- 9.9.0.2 ---\n\t\t\tMany BugFixes found in a code review (also released for FFmpeg 8 as 8.1.2.14):\n\t\t\tIO: custom IOContext callbacks are rooted and no longer let exceptions escape into native code; IOContext/CodecContext can be finalized; use-after-free when opening custom IO failed; IOStreamContext no longer throws on construction; seeking works for seekable IOContexts.\n\t\t\tFormats/Codecs: MuxerContext double dispose, NoFile check and time base rescaling; FormatContext.Seekable returns None without an I/O context again; extradata is padded as FFmpeg requires; SendFrame no longer changes an open encoder's time base; encoded subtitle packets use a correct time base; MediaSource keeps its decoders, drains all of them at end of file and SeekExactly ends only for the requested stream; seeks past ~35 minutes and timestamp setters past ~6.6 hours no longer overflow.\n\t\t\tUtils: Rational +, - and int * Rational overflow; TimeSpan / Rational saturated; AVPacket leak and Size overrun; AVFrame.GetData/Copy/Size/Clone for bottom-up and audio frames; AVBuffer.ReplaceWith use-after-free; Move/Clone/Reference onto itself emptied the packet; AVResult64.ToString named wrong errors.\n\t\t\tAudio: AudioFifo layout conversion and peeks beyond one chunk, pinning of channel spans; SwrContext wrote past the buffer when converting at an offset; AudioBuffer Copy/MakeWriteable shared data through stale plane pointers, planar-to-packed copies were wrong; AudioClock counted time twice after Pause; ChannelLayout.Init kept a freed map after a failure.\n\t\t\tCollections: CircularArray.IndexOf/Clear, AVChapter removal keeps its order, SubtitleRect text setters crashed, hardware device/frames context references crashed when empty.\n\t\t\tOptions: binary options were read from the wrong address; bool in SetOption(name, object); dictionary overloads use av_opt_set_dict2 and remove the entries that were set.\n\t\t\tMediaPlayer: VideoBuffer/AudioBuffer lost writes and CanSeek was reversed, AudioBuffer binary search could loop forever, SetBufferSize estimate, Stop state.\n\t\t\tMisc: SVTAV1.CreateAvif encoded the wrong frame; Transcoder decoded a packet twice; Logger kept no prefix state across av_log calls; FormatContext.Url is read as UTF-8; SwsContext throws if it cannot be created.\n\t\t\tBehaviour changes:\n\t\t\tTryGetOption(Option, out object): Color options are returned as string (\"0xRRGGBBAA\"), Duration as long (microseconds), array options as the string FFmpeg produces.\n\t\t\tSetOption(name, IDictionary) applies every entry as its own option (av_opt_set_dict2); `name` is not used.\n\t\t\tAudioBuffer.CopyTo/CopyToPacked throw ArgumentOutOfRangeException for a start index outside the buffer. SetBufferSize throws for a non-positive size or when no data rate can be determined.\n\t\t\tChannelLayout custom channel names must be shorter than 16 bytes (UTF-8).\n\t\t\tPlaybackEngine: a decoding error now moves the player to Faulted and raises Faulted, it was only logged before.\n\n\t\t\t--- 9.9.0.1 ---\n\t\t\tBugFix: - Fixed a bug concerning the incorrect size of CLong/CULong on Windows or 32bit and netstandard.\n\t\t\tSee AutoGen (v9.0.1.1) release notes for more details.",
